    32	
    33	## Construction (identical for all datasets)
    34	
    35	1. Load, clean, sort chronologically (stable sort); n = remaining rows.
    36	2. Binary label y = 1[target > median(target over rows [0, 0.30n))].
    37	3. Train-only `prep`: StandardScaler on numeric columns, OneHotEncoder(min_frequency=20,
    38	   handle_unknown="ignore") on categorical columns, both fit on rows [0, 0.30n).
    39	4. Incumbent: LogisticRegression(max_iter=300, C=1.0) fit on rows [0, 0.15n).
    40	   Challenger: HistGradientBoostingClassifier(max_iter=100, max_depth=4, learning_rate=0.1,
    41	   random_state=0) fit on rows [0, 0.30n).
    42	5. Episodes: K = min(20, floor((n - n30)/2000)) consecutive non-overlapping 2000-row windows
    43	   starting at n30 = int(0.30n). Losses l = 1[pred != y].
    44	
    45	## Per-dataset cleaning and features
    46	
    47	- **metro**: target `traffic_volume`; features holiday, weather_main, weather_description
    48	  (categorical), temp, rain_1h, snow_1h, clouds_all, plus hour/weekday/month from `date_time`
    49	  (then dropped). Note: 7629 rows share a timestamp with another row (one row per weather
    50	  description per hour, same traffic_volume); kept, as specified, so 24 events is slightly less
    51	  than one day on those hours.
    52	- **beijing_pm25**: target `pm2.5`; 2067 rows with missing target dropped. Features DEWP, TEMP,
    53	  PRES, Iws, Is, Ir, cbwd (categorical), hour/weekday/month. Dropped No, year, day.
    54	- **bike_hour**: target `cnt`; dropped casual and registered (they sum to cnt), instant, dteday,
    55	  yr (trend index); calendar re-derived. Features season, holiday, workingday, weathersit, temp,
    56	  atemp, hum, windspeed, hour/weekday/month.
    57	- **appliances**: target `Appliances` (Wh, 10-min); dropped date and rv1/rv2 (documented random
    58	  variables). Features lights, T1-T9, RH_1-RH_9, T_out, Press_mm_hg, RH_out, Windspeed,
    59	  Visibility, Tdewpoint, hour/weekday/month.
    60	- **household_power**: 1-min data ("?" = missing) resampled to 10-minute means; bins with no
    61	  complete reading dropped (n = 204950). Target `Global_active_power`. Dropped as leakage:
    62	  Global_intensity (about P/V) and Sub_metering_1-3 (contemporaneous components of the target).
    63	  Features Global_reactive_power, Voltage, hour/weekday/month.
    64	
    65	## Descriptive statistics (evaluator-side, not tuning inputs)
    66	
    67	Over all K episodes; advantage = mean(l0 - l1) per episode (positive: challenger better).
    68	
    69	| dataset | K | incumbent err | challenger err | disagreement | challenger better | eval pos. rate |
    70	|---|---|---|---|---|---|---|
    71	| metro | 16 | 0.360 | 0.047 | 0.360 | 16/16 | 0.510 |
    72	| beijing_pm25 | 14 | 0.332 | 0.260 | 0.207 | 13/14 | 0.497 |
    73	| bike_hour | 6 | 0.276 | 0.115 | 0.258 | 6/6 | 0.649 |
    74	| appliances | 6 | 0.411 | 0.259 | 0.432 | 6/6 | 0.464 |
    75	| household_power | 20 | 0.316 | 0.250 | 0.246 | 15/20 | 0.420 |
    76	
    77	Per-episode advantages are in `stats.json` (`mean_adv_per_episode`). The challenger is better
    78	in 56 of 62 episodes, so these streams mostly test whether a policy promotes a better challenger
    79	quickly and cheaply; only household_power (5/20) and beijing_pm25 (1/14) have harmful-switch
    80	episodes.
